### 2. Entanglement‑aware inverse propagation

Here we “rewind” the entanglement effects using the stored `last_delta_axis` and `last_delta_value`. This assumes forward used `+ ratio * delta`; inverse uses `- ratio * delta`.

Add this block near the top of `apply_10d_inverse_transform`, after loading `v_state`:

```sql
    ------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- 1b. Undo entanglement effects (inverse of PROC‑048)
    ------------------------------------------------------------------
    DECLARE
        v_last_axis TEXT;
        v_last_delta DOUBLE PRECISION;
        r_bond RECORD;
    BEGIN
        SELECT last_delta_axis, last_delta_value
        INTO v_last_axis, v_last_delta
        FROM ten_d_nodes
        WHERE id = in_node_id;

        IF v_last_axis IS NOT NULL THEN
            FOR r_bond IN
                SELECT * FROM entanglement_bonds
                WHERE node_id = in_node_id
                  AND source_dim = v_last_axis
            LOOP
                CASE r_bond.target_dim
                    WHEN 'x' THEN v_state[1] := v_state[1] - v_last_delta * r_bond.ratio;
                    WHEN 'y' THEN v_state[2] := v_state[2] - v_last_delta * r_bond.ratio;
                    WHEN 'z' THEN v_state[3] := v_state[3] - v_last_delta * r_bond.ratio;
                    WHEN 'w' THEN v_state[4] := v_state[4] - v_last_delta * r_bond.ratio;
                    WHEN 'v' THEN v_state[5] := v_state[5] - v_last_delta * r_bond.ratio;
